        "title": "Keep the turning direction",
        "text": "A simple DC motor uses a split-ring commutator and brushes to reverse current through the rotating coil every half-turn. This keeps the turning effect in the same rotational direction. The split ring is not two continuous slip rings used in an alternator.",
